{
 "format": "souls-form-cases/1",
 "about": "eden:radial_sculpture (from #1879). A portable wooden post of eight bands, 1 at the bottom to 8 at the top, each of radius 4 to begin with. Carving a band (three seconds, a hand free) takes it one radius thinner; it can never grow back and stops at 1, a solid core ('A cut must reduce that band radius; choose a smaller radius. Removed wood cannot be added back.'). Full hands refuse ('Empty your hands before carving the supported blank.'). The shavings are not a stored field: they are always 128 less the sum of the squared radii, so they are conserved by construction. Changed from the original: one cut is one radius (a cut from 4 to 2 is two acts), and the band is eight forms; a set whose field or value comes from an argument is a later format. Handed back: resting on a fixed work table, both hands empty, the maker credit replaced at each cut.",
